# implicit COMMIT (statement: DROP TABLE tf_ddl1): the boundary's statement opens and locks the tables whose triggers fire and the tables their bodies use
# implicit COMMIT (statement: DROP TABLE tf_ddl1): prelocking for test.tf: the bodies of the triggers that have rows to fire over (tf_commit) are prelocked by the boundary's statement
# implicit COMMIT (statement: DROP TABLE tf_ddl1): test.tf enters the firing chain at depth 1; it is open and locked by the boundary's statement, transactional MDL_SHARED_WRITE held: yes; bodies would run on the tables the boundary prelocked
# implicit COMMIT (statement: DROP TABLE tf_ddl1): FIRE test.tf_commit (AFTER INSERT BEFORE COMMIT, order 1) over positions [0, 2): 2 INSERT, 0 UPDATE, 0 DELETE rows; body would run here: execute_trigger() as root@localhost, SUB_STMT_TRIGGER
# transaction end: accumulator of 2 rows freed with the transaction mem_root
# prelocking for test.tf: INSERT BEFORE COMMIT triggers are prelocked by this statement
# column marking for test.tf: captured columns marked for read: a, + __op_order, __op, __state
# accumulator attached to thd->transaction (transaction mem_root)
# accumulator: new (transaction, table) entry for test.tf, columns: a, + __op_order, __op, __state; fixed from triggers tf_commit; has OR SAVEPOINT triggers: no
